+---
+id: dl-003-applypatch-replace-in-place-and-strict-patch-iteration
+type: decision-log
+title: "applyPatch replace in place and strict patch iteration"
+status: pending
+---
+
+<!-- decision-log body. `wingfoil memory add` copies this scaffold verbatim; `memory submit` replaces
+     these placeholder comments with real content and fills the required frontmatter fields. -->
+
+## Context
+
+Review of `applyPatch` against RFC 6902 showed `replace` reordered object members (remove then add) and a sparse patch array was accepted because `reduce` skips holes.
+
+## Decision
+
+- `replace` writes the new value at the existing location (array element or object member) without removing it.
+- The patch is iterated by index so every slot is validated, holes included.
+
+## Consequences
+
+Results of `replace` keep member order; sparse patches throw. No other behaviour of dl-002 changes.
